	How about amnesia resistance for Wizards? Just as Healers are
immune to potions of sickness, Wizards could be safe from losing 
memorized spells when they read a scroll of amnesia. (We could still
have them lose the map of the level, since that's pretty minor.) As
things are, it's very unsafe to read any spell book until you've found
a scroll of amnesia. If you don't find one until late in the game,
you've spent a lot of time as a magicless Wizard. Amnesia resistance
would encourage Wizards to read spell books, and make for a little
bit more differentiation between the character classes.

